      "url": "https://expressjs.com/en/guide/error-handling.html",
      "rationale": "Current official Express guide (v5.x tree); fetched 2026-09-08 and confirms verbatim: async/promise-returning handlers call next(value) automatically on reject/throw, while callback-based APIs (e.g. node:fs) are never part of a promise and must be forwarded to next(err) manually.",
